# ============================================================
# .assetsignore: what does NOT get uploaded to the edge.
#
# `[assets] directory = "./aab"` in wrangler.toml means every file
# in this folder is uploaded and served by Cloudflare at its own
# public URL. Every file: the checks, the tests, the two school
# builders and the TypeScript the served modules are compiled
# from were all live on reiad.co.uk, about 300 KB of them, at
# addresses like /check-routes.ts and /schema.sql.
#
# Nothing in them is secret. schema.sql is the shape of a database
# nobody can reach, the tests describe behaviour the site performs
# in public anyway, and the checks are the reason any of it works.
# It was still wrong twice over: they are not the site, and a file
# nobody meant to publish is a file nobody thinks about before
# changing.
#
# The rule is the same one the rest of this repository runs on.
# What is served is what a reader asks for. Everything below is
# how the site is built and checked, which is a question for a
# clone rather than for the edge.
#
# `scripts/check-routes.ts` reads this file and fails if a file
# matching one of these shapes is missing from it, so a new check
# or a new test cannot start being published by accident. It used
# to live here itself, which is why the first rule below exists
# and why it is now the weaker half of the answer: a check that is
# not in this directory cannot be served whatever this file says.
# ============================================================

# The builders. Run from a clone, never fetched.
#
# The five checks left this directory on 18 August 2026 and the
# `check-*.mjs` rule below now guards nothing that is here. It
# stays because the rule is cheap and the mistake is not: a check
# written beside these files again would be published by the next
# commit, and `scripts/check-routes.ts` fails on a build-or-test
# shape no rule covers, so the two together mean it cannot happen
# quietly either way.
#
# `build-meta.mjs` and `build-og.mjs` are still here. PLAN.md
# Phase 6 is what retires them: a sitemap and an OpenGraph image
# are both things Next has a better idiom for than a script.
# Both extensions, because these are being converted to
# TypeScript, which node runs directly. A rule that knew only
# `.mjs` would go quiet at the moment the files changed name, and
# `scripts/check-routes.ts` widened with it.
check-*.mjs
check-*.ts
build-*.mjs
build-*.ts
*/build-*.mjs
*/build-*.ts

# The tests. Same.
*.test.mjs
*.test.ts
*/*.test.mjs
*/*.test.ts

# One-off data fetchers, run by hand when a model needs refreshing.
portfolio/scorecard.fetch.mjs
portfolio/scorecard.fetch.ts

# The TypeScript that /api.js, /share-card.js, /photo.js and
# /tailwind.css are compiled from. The built files are served; the
# sources are not, and `scripts/build-modules.ts --check` is what
# keeps the two honest.
src/

# The database's shape, applied with wrangler from a clone.
schema.sql

# The design harness. `scripts/preview.ts` writes it: one of every
# surface, button, chip and field in all seven sections, against
# the real stylesheets, so a change to the palette can be LOOKED
# at rather than reasoned about. It is generated, it is not a page
# of this site, and it is regenerated rather than edited.
preview.html
